built_from: a1536bc6 (S83 tip, = HEAD when this artifact was built at S82)
  RECORDED AT S84, because from S84 this artifact no longer rebuilds from
  HEAD and the only thing that said which commit it came from was "HEAD at
  the time". The label IS the source hash -- sha256 over the slot-map hash,
  the CFG_LINE, rtl/*.v, the qsf and the sdc, first 12 chars -- so it can be
  checked WITHOUT Quartus, in one line, at any commit:

    git -C <repo> stash list >/dev/null   # clean tree, then at that commit:
    cd shared/dsp4-logic && cat \
      <(grep -o 'sha256:[0-9a-f]*' generated/dsp4_slot_map.vh | head -1) \
      <(echo "loopback=0 pi_selftest=0 pi_maincap=0 pi_tdm8=0 drive_all=0") \
      rtl/*.v quartus/dsp4_logic.qsf quartus/dsp4_logic.sdc \
      | sha256sum | cut -c1-12
    # -> 7a6a4529f29c at a1536bc6 and at every commit up to it.

  Note the CFG_LINE above has no `ad_witness=` term: that term is added at
  S84, so the one-liner for THIS artifact is the five-switch form and the
  one for anything built after S84 is the six-switch form. That is the whole
  reason the label moved.

why_it_moved: S84 added the ad[0..2] witness to rtl/ under DSP4_AD_WITNESS
  (default OFF) to answer S83-Q1. SRC_HASH covers rtl/*.v wholesale and
  cannot tell a guarded addition from a behavioural change, so the shipping
  build's label moves from 7a6a4529f29c to 0cc6f94444b2 even though the
  shipping PATH is unchanged and the sim gate passes on it. THIS artifact --
  the one on the part -- is not affected: it is still the bytes it always
  was, it still answers 32'h4529f29c, and it is still the shipping bitstream.
  Whether shipping ADOPTS 0cc6f94444b2 (and re-checks the S82 84.34 % D24
  capacity row on it) is the hub's call; S84 did not make it.
